gdbserver on m68k, asked for its target description.

m68k's gdbserver describes its registers only through the regformats
table (reg-m68k.dat): no XML file and no features. It still advertises
qXfer:features:read -- every gdbserver does -- and when GDB asked for
target.xml it failed an internal assertion and exited, so no remote
session could start. With neither form of description it now answers
that there is none, and GDB uses m68k's default register set.

diff -ru a/gdbserver/server.cc b/gdbserver/server.cc
--- a/gdbserver/server.cc	2026-10-01 08:35:31.232787391 -0600
+++ b/gdbserver/server.cc	2026-10-01 08:35:31.279338746 -0600
@@ -1132,6 +1132,15 @@
 
   if (strcmp (annex, "target.xml") == 0)
     {
+      /* A target with neither -- m68k's register set is only the
+	 regformats table -- has no description to give.  Say so, and
+	 GDB uses the architecture's default registers, as it would
+	 with a stub that never offered one.  */
+      if (desc->xmltarget == NULL
+	  && (desc->features.empty ()
+	      || tdesc_architecture_name (desc) == nullptr))
+	return NULL;
+
       const char *ret = tdesc_get_features_xml (desc);
 
       if (*ret == '@')
